#!/bin/sh
# wanguard-antidpi - control CLI (issue #57). Single control surface for the
# nfqws2 engine: the init script drives it, the container test matrix (#63)
# asserts against it, blockcheck sessions read the exact engine command line.
#
# Subcommands:
#   version         package version stamp (default action)
#   engine-version  first line of `nfqws2 --version`
#   engine-cmdline  full nfqws2 argv, one argument per line
#   nft-render      print the rendered nft ruleset (template + config QNUM)
#   nft-apply       apply the table (idempotent; DRYRUN-aware)
#   nft-flush       delete the table (idempotent; DRYRUN-aware)
#
# DRYRUN contract: WANGUARD_ANTIDPI_DRYRUN=1 makes every state-changing
# command print what it would do, touch nothing, exit 0. This is how the
# container matrix tests the scripts without live nft/queue state.
#
# Config: /etc/wanguard-antidpi/config (sh-style, sourced with `.`).
set -u

BASE=/usr/share/wanguard-antidpi
NFT_TEMPLATE="$BASE/wanguard-antidpi.nft"
TABLE=wanguard_antidpi
CONFIG=/etc/wanguard-antidpi/config
ENGINE=/usr/bin/nfqws2

load_config() {
	[ -r "$CONFIG" ] || { echo "wanguard-antidpi: config not readable: $CONFIG" >&2; exit 1; }
	# shellcheck disable=SC1090
	. "$CONFIG"
	: "${QNUM:=300}"
	: "${DESYNC_MARK:=0x40000000}"
	: "${WS_USER:=daemon}"
	: "${NFQWS2_DEBUG:=0}"
}

cmd_version() {
	V="$BASE/version"
	[ -r "$V" ] || { echo "wanguard-antidpi: no version stamp installed" >&2; exit 1; }
	echo "wanguard-antidpi $(cat "$V")"
}

cmd_engine_version() {
	[ -x "$ENGINE" ] || { echo "wanguard-antidpi: engine not installed: $ENGINE" >&2; exit 1; }
	"$ENGINE" --version 2>/dev/null | head -n 1
}

cmd_engine_cmdline() {
	load_config
	echo "$ENGINE"
	echo "--qnum=$QNUM"
	echo "--fwmark=$DESYNC_MARK"
	echo "--user=$WS_USER"
	# gzipped lua is supported natively by nfqws2 (--lua-init=@<file>)
	echo "--lua-init=@$BASE/lua/zapret-lib.lua.gz"
	echo "--lua-init=@$BASE/lua/zapret-antidpi.lua.gz"
	[ "$NFQWS2_DEBUG" = "1" ] && echo "--debug=1"
	# strategy: word-split (config contract: no quoted-space arguments);
	# empty NFQWS2_OPT = engine idles and passes queued packets unmodified
	for w in $NFQWS2_OPT; do
		echo "$w"
	done
}

cmd_nft_render() {
	load_config
	[ -r "$NFT_TEMPLATE" ] || { echo "wanguard-antidpi: nft template missing: $NFT_TEMPLATE" >&2; exit 1; }
	sed "s/@QNUM@/$QNUM/g" "$NFT_TEMPLATE"
}

cmd_nft_apply() {
	load_config
	if [ "${WANGUARD_ANTIDPI_DRYRUN:-0}" = "1" ]; then
		echo "DRYRUN: would apply nft table inet $TABLE:"
		cmd_nft_render
		return 0
	fi
	tmp="${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/wanguard-antidpi.nft.$$"
	cmd_nft_render > "$tmp"
	nft -f "$tmp"
	rc=$?
	rm -f "$tmp"
	logger -t wanguard-antidpi "nft table inet $TABLE applied (queue $QNUM)"
	return $rc
}

cmd_nft_flush() {
	load_config
	if [ "${WANGUARD_ANTIDPI_DRYRUN:-0}" = "1" ]; then
		echo "DRYRUN: would delete nft table inet $TABLE"
		return 0
	fi
	# idempotent: a missing table is not an error on stop
	nft delete table inet "$TABLE" 2>/dev/null || true
	logger -t wanguard-antidpi "nft table inet $TABLE flushed"
}

case "${1:-version}" in
	version)          cmd_version ;;
	engine-version)   cmd_engine_version ;;
	engine-cmdline)   cmd_engine_cmdline ;;
	nft-render)       cmd_nft_render ;;
	nft-apply)        cmd_nft_apply ;;
	nft-flush)        cmd_nft_flush ;;
	*)
		echo "usage: wanguard-antidpi [version|engine-version|engine-cmdline|nft-render|nft-apply|nft-flush]" >&2
		exit 2
		;;
esac
